________________________________________
Lesson 4: How Does One Computer Send Bits?
Imagine two computers.
PC A ---------------- PC B
Question:
How can electricity represent data?
Let's define:
5 Volts = 1
0 Volts = 0
Then
1010
can be transmitted as
5V
0V
5V
0V
This is the foundation of networking.
Everything eventually becomes electrical or optical signals.
________________________________________
Lesson 5: Physical Medium
Computers cannot throw bits through the air magically.
They need a medium.
Copper Cable
PC ---- Ethernet Cable ---- Switch
Signal is electrical.
________________________________________
Fiber Optic
PC ---- Fiber ---- Network
Signal is light.
Much faster.
Used in:
•	ISPs
•	Data Centers
•	Cloud Providers
________________________________________
Wireless
Laptop ))))) WiFi ))))) Router
Signal is radio waves.
Still carrying 1s and 0s.
________________________________________
